# 1. SIGNALCLOUD ENGINE FAMILY

Estimated professional replacement labor:

```text
850–1,350 hours
~$49.5k–$78.6k wage-equivalent
```

This is the largest Window B work family, but it is not the entire Window B audit.

Counted work includes the Window B implementation and refinement represented by such areas as:

- engine/runtime work;
- authoring and studio tooling;
- native stress and recovery systems;
- machine-profile and runtime validation;
- SCFONT-related tooling;
- Asset Doctor and asset-validation work;
- environment and material/light tooling;
- public-core / portable-core preparation;
- privacy and release-surface cleanup;
- release manifests and verification;
- Linux packaging and launch paths;
- integration and repeated acceptance testing.

Important boundary:

```text
Bitninja Mocap Lite itself was already paid for in Window A.

Window B counts only NEW SignalCloud-side integration,
avatar/native pipeline work, and later systems.
```

SignalCloud receives the largest hour range because the development record contains a broad runtime/tooling/release surface with repeated test and acceptance cycles.

The estimate does **not** assume that the entire engine was invented from zero during these 65 days.

It estimates the Window B work that was actually performed.

