# FINAL AUDIT STATEMENT

The performed-work record supports treating Window B as a substantially larger professional replacement-work inventory than Window A while preserving the original audit's pricing lens.

The best-supported public-facing number is therefore:

```text
WINDOW B:
approximately $130,000–$214,000
in wage-equivalent professional replacement labor

midpoint:
approximately $172,000
```

This result counts public, private, and incomplete work only through the boundary actually performed and evidenced during the period.

It excludes Window A rebuilds, future planned work, unsupported commercial valuation, and failed work with no sufficiently reusable/testable result.

The headline is replacement labor.

It is not resale value.

It is not "AI did everything."

It is not time travel.

It is an estimate of the professional work represented by what was actually built, tested, debugged, documented, packaged, integrated, or coached during the 65-day Window B period.
